Experiment No. 2
Problem Identification and Feasibility: Software Design Principles


Aim

To identify the problem addressed by the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform and prepare its problem statement, objectives, scope, and technical and operational feasibility analysis.


Objectives
1.To identify the real-world cybersecurity problem addressed by the proposed software project.
2.To prepare a clear and well-defined problem statement.
3.To define the objectives and scope of the project.
4.To perform technical and operational feasibility analysis.
5.To evaluate the viability of the proposed solution.

Introduction

Problem identification is one of the most important stages of software engineering. Before developing a software system, it is necessary to understand the real-world problem that the system intends to solve.

A well-defined problem statement helps developers understand the requirements and expectations of users. Similarly, a feasibility study helps determine whether the proposed software solution is practical, technically possible, and operationally acceptable.

With the increasing use of digital platforms, cyber threats such as phishing attacks have become a major concern. Many users are unable to identify suspicious emails, fake websites, malicious links, and fraudulent messages. Lack of cybersecurity awareness increases the possibility of users becoming victims of cyber attacks.

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform aims to address this problem by providing interactive training, phishing simulations, quizzes, and performance-based awareness assessment.



Selected Project
Project Title

Cybersecurity Awareness Platform for Phishing Detection and Prevention

Domain

Cybersecurity and Information Security


Problem Statement

Phishing attacks are one of the most common cybersecurity threats faced by internet users. Attackers often use fake emails, fraudulent websites, malicious links, and deceptive messages to steal sensitive information such as usernames, passwords, banking details, and personal data.

Many users lack sufficient knowledge and practical experience to identify phishing attempts. Traditional cybersecurity awareness methods are often limited to theoretical information and do not provide users with practical experience in recognizing real-world phishing attacks.

Therefore, there is a need for an interactive Cybersecurity Awareness Platform that helps users learn how to identify and prevent phishing attacks through educational content, realistic phishing simulations, interactive quizzes, and performance-based awareness assessment.

The proposed system will provide a practical learning environment where users can improve their ability to recognize suspicious activities and develop better cybersecurity awareness.

Project Objectives

The main objectives of the proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform are:

1.To provide cybersecurity awareness training to users.
2.To educate users about phishing attacks and common phishing techniques.
3.To simulate realistic phishing scenarios for practical learning.
4.To help users identify suspicious emails, links, and websites.
5.To conduct interactive quizzes to evaluate user knowledge.
6.To assess user performance based on training and quiz results.
7.To provide feedback to help users improve their cybersecurity awareness.
8.To develop a secure, user-friendly, and interactive platform.


Project Scope

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform focuses on improving user awareness and knowledge related to phishing attacks.

The system includes the following features:

User Training

Users can access educational content related to phishing attacks, suspicious emails, fake websites, malicious links, social engineering techniques, and cybersecurity best practices.

Phishing Simulations

The system will provide realistic and safe phishing scenarios where users can practice identifying suspicious emails, fake URLs, malicious links, and fraudulent websites.

Interactive Quizzes

Users can attempt quizzes related to cybersecurity and phishing awareness. These quizzes will help evaluate the user's understanding and ability to identify suspicious activities.

Performance Assessment

The system will analyze user performance based on quiz scores, simulation results, correct and incorrect answers, and overall awareness level.

Feedback

The platform will provide feedback to users so that they can understand their mistakes and improve their cybersecurity awareness.



Out of Scope

The following features are outside the scope of the current project:

Real-time antivirus software.
Malware removal.
Network intrusion detection.
Firewall development.
Execution of real phishing attacks.
Digital forensic investigation.


Technical Feasibility Analysis

Technical feasibility analysis determines whether the proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform can be developed using the available technologies, hardware, software tools, and technical resources.

The proposed system is technically feasible because modern web technologies and development tools are readily available and suitable for developing a web-based cybersecurity awareness platform.

Factor | Assessment | Remarks
Technology | Feasible | Modern web technologies can be used for development
Frontend | Feasible | HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and React.js can be used
Backend | Feasible | Node.js and Express.js can be used
Database | Feasible | MongoDB can be used to store application data
Hardware | Feasible | Standard computers are sufficient for development and testing
Software Tools | Feasible | VS Code, Git, GitHub, and Postman are available
Security | Feasible | Authentication and secure data handling can be implemented
Scalability | Feasible | Modular architecture supports future expansion


Technology Feasibility

The proposed system can be developed using modern and commonly available web technologies.

The frontend of the application can be developed using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and React.js. These technologies can be used to create an interactive and user-friendly interface.

The backend can be developed using Node.js and Express.js. These technologies can handle application logic, user requests, authentication, and communication with the database.

MongoDB can be used as the database to store user information, quiz data, training content, simulation results, and performance records.

These technologies are widely used, well documented, and suitable for the development of the proposed system.


Hardware Feasibility

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform does not require expensive or specialized hardware.

A standard computer system with the following resources is sufficient:

- A computer or laptop with a standard processor.
- Basic memory and storage capacity.
- Internet connection.
- A web browser.

Therefore, the project is feasible from a hardware perspective.


Software Tools Feasibility

The required software development tools are easily available and suitable for developing the proposed system.

The following tools can be used:

- Visual Studio Code for software development.
- Git for version control.
- GitHub for source code management and team collaboration.
- MongoDB for database management.
- Postman for API testing.
- UML tools for system design and documentation.

Most of these tools are freely available or open source. Therefore, the required software resources are easily accessible.


Security Feasibility

The proposed system can implement basic security mechanisms to protect user information and application data.

Possible security measures include:

- User authentication.
- Secure password storage.
- Input validation.
- Access control.
- Secure communication between the application and database.
- Protection of user information.

Since the project focuses on cybersecurity awareness, secure software development practices should be followed during implementation.


Scalability Feasibility

The proposed system can be designed using a modular architecture.

The application can contain separate modules such as:

- User Authentication Module.
- Training Module.
- Phishing Simulation Module.
- Quiz Module.
- Performance Assessment Module.

This modular structure makes the system easier to maintain and allows new features to be added in the future.

Possible future enhancements include:

- Advanced phishing simulations.
- Administrator dashboard.
- User performance analytics.
- Certificate generation.
- Personalized learning recommendations.

Therefore, the proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform is technically feasible and scalable.






Analysis

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform addresses the growing problem of phishing attacks and the lack of cybersecurity awareness among users.

The system provides an educational and practical environment where users can learn about phishing attacks and practice identifying suspicious activities. Interactive simulations and quizzes can improve user engagement compared to traditional theoretical awareness methods.

The technical and operational feasibility analysis indicates that the project can be successfully implemented using available technologies and resources.


Observation

Clearly defining the problem, objectives, scope, and feasibility requirements provides a strong foundation for software design and development.

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform is focused on solving a real-world problem by improving users' ability to recognize and prevent phishing attacks.



Result

The problem statement, project objectives, project scope, and feasibility requirements for the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform were successfully identified and prepared.

The proposed solution is practical and provides an effective approach for improving cybersecurity awareness related to phishing detection and prevention.